{
  "name": "Arena -- Verona, ground and second storey",
  "_about": "Verona's amphitheatre at its real scale, as a circle (the ellipse comes later): 69.4m to the facade, 58.4m to the inner ring, a 30.2m arena, 40 rows from a 4m podium to 22m, two 11m storeys of arcade whose second extrados arrives at 22m -- the deck of the upper level and the top row are the same line.\\nTHE THREE FLIGHTS, as the Renaissance section of the building shows them. From the ground ambulatory a stair climbs inward under the seating and opens at row 12, the middle of the lower half. From the same ambulatory another climbs ALONG the ring to the second floor -- eleven metres will not fit in a six-metre corridor going outward, which is why the real ones turn. From the second floor a passage runs straight in and a third flight opens at row 32, the middle of the upper half.\\nWHAT IS DRAWN. Almost none of this building is drawn as a solid. The cavea is 28 metres of concrete whose only visible surfaces are the steps on top of it, the soffit over each tunnel and the walls that tunnel runs between, so that is what the parts emit -- `faces`. Passages use the `parallel` plan, which runs them out along one ray at a fixed width instead of cutting a wedge that would be half again as wide at the facade as at the arena, and their width is the arch they pass through.\\nEvery radius sits on the row lattice and every height on a row: the rows are 70.5cm deep because 47 stair treads of 30cm then measure exactly 20 rows, and 45cm high on a 4m podium because 47 risers of exactly 20cm then arrive at row 12. The upper flight's 37 risers of 20cm arrive at row 32 for the same reason.",
  "params": {
    "bays": 60,
    "detail": 8,
    "rOuter": 69.4,
    "wallT": 2.6,
    "corridorW": 6.0,
    "innerT": 2.4,
    "rOuterInner": "rOuter - wallT - corridorW",
    "rInnerFace": "rOuterInner - innerT",
    "storeyH": 11.0,
    "_storeyH": "two storeys of 11m put the second extrados at 22m, which is where the top row of seating arrives",
    "openW": 4.4,
    "springing": 5.4,
    "archCrown": "springing + openW / 2",
    "innerOpenW": 3.6,
    "innerSpringing": 4.8,
    "vaultRise": 2.2,
    "pathW": "innerOpenW",
    "_pathW": "every passage is as wide as the arch it comes through, and parallel-sided from end to end",
    "rArena": 30.2,
    "podium": 4.0,
    "podiumT": 0.6,
    "caveaRows": 40,
    "caveaTop": 20.0,
    "rCavea": "rInnerFace",
    "rowRun": "(rCavea - rArena) / caveaRows",
    "rowRise": "(caveaTop - podium) / caveaRows",
    "stairRise": 0.2,
    "stairRun": 0.25,
    "vomEvery": 5,
    "emergeRow": 12,
    "mouthRow": 15,
    "passEndRow": 28,
    "_emergeRow": "44 steps of exactly 20cm from the ground reach the 4m podium plus twelve 40cm rows (8.8m)",
    "rEmerge": "rArena + emergeRow * rowRun",
    "rMouth": "rArena + mouthRow * rowRun",
    "rPassEnd": "rArena + passEndRow * rowRun",
    "caveaAtEmerge": "podium + emergeRow * rowRise",
    "tunnelHead": "podium + mouthRow * rowRise",
    "caveaAtPassEnd": "podium + passEndRow * rowRise",
    "passHead": 2.6,
    "_passHead": "the level stretch of a vomitorium is 2.6m under the seating -- a low entrance, against 7.6m to the crown of an arcade arch",
    "emergeRow2": 28,
    "mouthRow2": 31,
    "_emergeRow2": "the upper flight begins only once it is out of the arcade and climbs within the cavea's mass: 21 risers of exactly 20cm from the second floor (11m) reach row 28 (15.2m)",
    "rEmerge2": "rArena + emergeRow2 * rowRun",
    "rMouth2": "rArena + mouthRow2 * rowRun",
    "caveaAtEmerge2": "podium + emergeRow2 * rowRise",
    "tunnelHead2": "podium + mouthRow2 * rowRise",
    "stairFoot2": "rEmerge2 + (caveaAtEmerge2 - storeyH) / stairRise * stairRun",
    "flightW": "innerOpenW",
    "_flightW": "a flight is as wide as the arch it leaves through, so its tunnel walls run flush with the arch's jambs",
    "stairA": 28,
    "stairB": 27,
    "landingY": "stairA * stairRise",
    "landingDepth": 3.0,
    "landingHead": 2.6,
    "levelRow": 18,
    "levelHeadRow": 24,
    "_levelRow": "the second floor is 11m and row 18 is 11.2m, so the path from it runs in dead level and opens there; the seating needs six rows to rise a head's height over it, so that is how long its mouth is",
    "rLevel": "rArena + levelRow * rowRun",
    "yLevel": "podium + levelRow * rowRise",
    "rLevelHead": "rArena + levelHeadRow * rowRun",
    "yLevelHead": "podium + levelHeadRow * rowRise",
    "rStairOut": "rInnerFace",
    "_rStairOut": "the switchback is FULLY PAST the arcade: it starts at the face of the inner ring and both its halves are inside the cavea's own mass, so the ambulatory keeps its vault and its arches all the way round",
    "rStairIn": "rStairOut - stairA * stairRun",
    "stairRunB": "(rStairOut - rStairIn) / stairB",
    "_stairRunB": "the return flight has one riser fewer than the first (28 + 27 of 20cm is the 11m storey), so its treads are 25.9cm rather than 25 -- which is what makes both halves span the same 7m and land the top exactly at the floor above",
    "rLandIn": "rStairIn - landingDepth",
    "rLandArc": "rStairIn - landingDepth / 2",
    "landingArc": "(2 * 3.14159265 * rStairIn / bays + flightW) * rLandArc / rStairIn",
    "_landingArc": "a bay of arc PLUS a flight's width, measured where the flights meet it: a landing one bay wide reaches only their centre lines and leaves half of each hanging",
    "soffitA": "landingY + landingHead",
    "soffitB": "storeyH + landingHead",
    "backWallArc": "(2 * 3.14159265 * rStairIn / bays - flightW) * rLandArc / rStairIn",
    "_mouthRow": "the mouth is where the tunnel's sloping ceiling -- a head's height over the flight -- breaks through the seating: three rows above the row the stair arrives at",
    "stairSlope": "stairRise / stairRun",
    "ceilAtMouth": "caveaAtEmerge + tunnelHeadroom - (rMouth - rEmerge) * stairSlope",
    "tunnelHeadroom": "passHead",
    "ceilAtMouth2": "caveaAtEmerge2 + tunnelHeadroom - (rMouth2 - rEmerge2) * stairSlope",
    "lintelTop": "innerSpringing + innerOpenW / 2 + 0.4",
    "_lintelTop": "just over the crown of an inner-arcade arch: what closes the wall between a low tunnel and the tall arch it is entered through",
    "_caveaTop": "40 rows of 40cm on the 4m podium: a seat is ~40cm high and ~70cm deep (here 70.5), so the top row stands at 20m and the upper arcade's last 2m are the wall behind it",
    "stairFoot": "rEmerge + caveaAtEmerge / stairRise * stairRun",
    "_stairFoot": "where the lower flight starts: 44 treads of 25cm (11m) out from the row it arrives at. The level passage runs from there to the arcade.",
    "_stairRun": "an inner stair is 20cm on a 25cm tread -- steeper than the seating it runs under (40 on 70.5)"
  },
